 :why-one-landing-and-not-two
 "blockification ALONE regresses geometry: :flex/nested-flex drops from 5/5
  boxes to 3/5 (1652 -> 1650). The engine had been getting a row flex
  container's max-content right BY ACCIDENT -- its items carried no
  `display`, so they looked inline and were summed. Blockifying them makes
  them look like blocks, and the block rule takes the MAX. The correct rule
  is that a row flex container's max-content is the SUM of its items plus
  main-axis gaps (the max only along a column). The counterfactual run is
  the evidence: sizing fix alone = 0 per-case deltas anywhere; both
  together = 0 geometry/line/paint deltas and +39 computed style.
  This is the earlier withdrawal (2026-08-04) landed correctly."
 :design
 "flex-item-main-width gained a branch keyed on the box's OWN display,
  placed before the inline branches -- a flex container's items are
  blockified whatever they were written as. block-max-content-width's
  per-child measurement was extracted to a shared
  `child-outer-max-content-width` so the max rule and the sum rule cannot
  drift. That is the only shared helper touched."
 :cost
 "cascade DOM ops over the whole corpus 20000 -> 20035 (+35 :style/display
  set-attr ops, +0.18%). The 39 changed values minus 35 new ops = the four
  elements (button x2, input x2) whose UA inline-block becomes block -- a
  value change, not an extra op. This is the measured cost the
  ADR-2800003100 estimate anticipated."
