 :design
 "the rename is ONE `map` over resolve-style-for's already-sorted
  declaration list, below the sort and above the group-by. The cascade
  already sorts by importance/origin/inline/layer/specificity/order and
  takes the last of each property group; renaming logical->physical IN THAT
  LIST makes every row of the order table above fall out with NO ORDERING
  CODE AT ALL. The element's flow {:writing-mode :direction} is threaded
  down run-cascade-walk like parent-font-size / parent-display already
  were. Because it happens inside the cascade, margin-inline-start: 2em and
  margin-inline: var(--gap) 5px needed no new entries anywhere -- they
  reach resolve-relative-lengths / resolve-style-map already wearing
  physical names (verified against Brave: 40px and 25px)."
 :percentages-one-fix-did-not-cover-gaps
 {:answer "no -- three properties spelled 50%, three bases"
  :margin-padding "containing block's INLINE size, all four sides. Fixed
                   here: node-style now carries the raw value beside the
                   coerced one -- the same thing it already did for
                   margin's `auto`, for the same reason -- and
                   resolve-box-percentages rewrites the map once at the
                   sites that know that size. That fixes all ~56 call sites
                   of margin-side/inset-side WITHOUT TOUCHING ONE."
  :inset "top/left/right/bottom resolve against the containing block's size
          in the value's OWN axis (left:50% of 200x60 is 100, top:50% is
          30). These ALREADY AGREED -- an earlier round did land them --
          and are untouched."
  :row-gap "the container's own content BLOCK size, which for an
            auto-height container is CYCLIC: measured, a 10% row gap on a
            40px-tall auto grid is 4px AND THE CONTAINER STAYS 40 TALL --
            resolved against a height computed without it, content
            overflowing. That is a two-pass rule and its own round. The two
            :gap/ cases are unchanged."}
 :scope-cuts
 [{:what "writing-mode -- the rename is GATED on horizontal-tb"
   :measured "under vertical-rl: inline-size:70px; block-size:20px is a box
              20 WIDE x 70 TALL (engine: 300x20); margin-inline-start:40px
              is a MARGIN-TOP; padding-block-start:12px is a PADDING-RIGHT;
              padding-top:10% of a 200-tall parent is 20px (basis = inline
              size = the height)."
   :why "adding four rotated rows would make getComputedStyle right while
